Q6. In-Memory Vector L2 Normalization
Topics: Embeddings

Task: Write a pure NumPy utility function to L2 normalize high-dimensional dense embedding vectors to prepare them for inner product / cosine distance calculations.

Solution Architecture:

    import numpy as np
    from typing import Union

    def l2_normalize(vectors: np.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-12) -> np.ndarray:
        """
        Performs L2 normalization on a 1D vector or a 2D matrix of embeddings.
        When vectors are L2-normalized, dot product equals cosine similarity.
        """
        arr = np.asarray(vectors, dtype=np.float32)
        
        if arr.ndim == 1:
            norm = np.linalg.norm(arr)
            return arr / max(norm, eps)
        
        elif arr.ndim == 2:
            norms = np.linalg.norm(arr, axis=1, keepdims=True)
            norms = np.maximum(norms, eps)
            return arr / norms
        
        else:
            raise ValueError(f"Expected 1D or 2D array, got {arr.ndim}D array.")
